# sqlplus (OCI thick, Instant Client) calling
#   PROCEDURE dbbat_cap_refcur(p OUT SYS_REFCURSOR)
# through dbbat against Oracle 23ai Free. One line per server response that
# opens with the IO vector (TTC message 0x0b): the TNS Data payload, two
# data-flag bytes first, exactly as extractTTCPayload receives it.
#
# These are the same REF cursor descriptors the thin recordings carry, marshaled
# in the wide/fixed-width OCI encoding — four-byte little-endian integers where a
# thin client sends compressed ones. refCursorIDsInBindOutput refuses them at the
# first field rather than reading a number out of the wrong encoding, which is
# what TestOCIRefCursorBindOutputYieldsNoID pins.
#
# Regenerate with:
#   go test -tags capture -run TestCapture_SQLPlusRefCursor ./internal/proxy/oracle/


